# `const A = B => class extends B { .. }`, `class M extends A(R) {}`, `new M(r)`: the object is born in the constructor of R, taken in line behind the tests of the two parents, and new.target is known to be M.
# The birth was given the class of new.target only where a row of WRITTEN bases led from it up to the class whose constructor allocates. Past a parent that is a value it stayed an object of no known layout, made out of
# line below the prototype that new.target names, and was asked for its shape at the first store.
# The run itself makes an instance of the class that the prototype names wherever that class has a parent that is no proven layout (ClassTable::instanceWithPrototype()). The walk says the same where the parents that the
# class records name lead up to the class of the allocation.
# f1 = f, f2 = g . L0 = the class in A, L1 = R, L2 = M
# -- source: an-object-born-above-a-mixin-is-of-the-class-that-new-target-names.cjs
